      "writtenOn": "2019-10-02T01:18:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "oh, this is quirky: our desktop \"gcc -m32\" is happy with %d.\nthe coreboot i386-elf-gcc is not happy (surprise!).\ndesktop \"gcc -m64\" is also not happy (expected).\n\nmy suggestion is to support %td instead of forcing 64bit promotion/arithmetic on tiny 32 bit machines.  i assume\nthis is essentially the same case as %zd in the printf implementation?",
